mintcam (0.2.4) noble; urgency=medium

  * Fix a crash in the preview loop: an exception raised by any per-frame step
    (filter, face framing, motion detection, recorder, streaming) escaped
    _update_preview and took the application down, because PyQt aborts the
    process when a slot raises. The pipeline is now guarded, the error is
    logged with the frame count, and the preview stops visibly after ten
    consecutive failures instead of dying silently.
  * Fix the face auto-framing, which never worked on this system: the Haar
    cascade is shipped in the separate opencv-data package, while the code
    looked for it in cv2.data, which the Ubuntu opencv build does not expose.
    The cascade is now looked up in the pip location and in the Debian/Ubuntu
    paths, opencv-data is a dependency, and the classifier is built once
    instead of on every frame.
  * When the face framing cannot work for any reason it now disables itself
    after five attempts and says why, instead of doing nothing on every frame.
  * Show an error dialog when recording with audio is requested but ffmpeg is
    not installed, instead of failing silently.
  * Tests: 3 regression tests for the preview guard and 1 for the face framing
    fallback.

 -- Alex Mirici <hilliedmikerano@gmail.com>  Mon, 12 Oct 2026 13:20:00 +0200

